statement:
Someone writes a three-stage shift register:

```verilog
always @(posedge clk) begin
    q1 = d;
    q2 = q1;
    q3 = q2;
end
```

They expected `d` to take three clock cycles to reach `q3`, with `q1`, `q2` and `q3` holding the last three input values.

**What does the synthesiser actually produce?**
